Generate a Next.js + Tailwind CSS multi-page, modern, responsive portfolio website for a web developer named Adamanth. It should be optimized for free hosting on Vercel.

Pages and Content:

Home Page: Hero section with the name “Adamanth” and the motto “Turning complex code into simple, stunning experiences.” Add a button linking to the Projects page.

About Page: A short bio: “I’m Adamanth, a web developer who loves making the strange and complex feel approachable. I thrive on creative problem-solving, blending clean code with thoughtful design. My work is all about building digital experiences that are functional, engaging, and a little bit unexpected.” Below it, add a Skills section with cards for: React, Next.js, Tailwind CSS, TypeScript, Node.js, Express, PostgreSQL, APIs (REST & GraphQL), Docker, Git/GitHub, and AI integrations.

Projects Page: Placeholder project cards with titles, short descriptions, and “Coming Soon” buttons.

Resume Page: A section with a “Download Resume” button. The button should link to a placeholder PDF file.

Testimonials Page: Placeholder section with “Testimonials coming soon” in styled cards.

Contact Page: Include email and Facebook icons with links.

Design Requirements:

Dark theme, modern styling, responsive across devices.

Smooth animations and hover effects.

Navigation bar with links to each page.

Responsive design that works great on desktop, tablet, and mobile.

Use Tailwind utilities for styling consistency.

The output should be a Next.js project structure ready to be pushed to GitHub and deployed on Vercel for free.